# .reviewlooprc — what this repo adds to /review-loop

Copy this file to `.reviewlooprc` at your repo's root and fill in what applies. Every section is
optional; delete the ones you do not need. The file is prose: the skill reads it in full before
its first round. It adds your repo's conventions and cannot loosen a rule of the skill.

## Read first

<!-- The documents every lens reads, by path, and the ones to read only when a diff touches
their area. -->

## Checks and shared services

<!-- How to run the tests and checks. What a reviewer must not touch: a shared database, a live
deployment, a real account, a command that rewrites files. -->

## Lens angles

### Correctness

<!-- Angles in your stack's terms: the error paths that matter here, the callers on the other
side of a contract. -->

### Adversarial

<!-- The hostile inputs, races and leaks this codebase is prone to. -->

### API design

<!-- What the contract is here, the naming rules, the boundaries that must hold. -->

### Test rigor

<!-- What a test here must prove, and how concurrency or platform claims are shown. -->

## Fixing

<!-- Rules a fix must follow, and the documents a fix can make false. -->

## Gated areas

<!-- What each of the skill's four gated areas means in this repo, and any area you add:
Stated principles; Private data and secrets; Stored data and published contracts; Money. -->

## Reporting

<!-- Where follow-up work is filed, and the parent issue for pre-existing findings if you keep
one. -->
